 ```
 
+#### Max Losing Streak
+
+`MaxLosingStreak` tracks consecutive losing trades - not overall profit - within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`). It locks trading as soon as the most recent `trade_limit` trades in a row all resulted in a loss, regardless of any winning trades further in the past. A single winning (or break-even) trade resets the streak.
+
+By default, this evaluates trades across all pairs to detect a bot-wide losing streak. Set `only_per_pair` to `true` to disable the bot-wide (global) check and only track streaks individually per pair.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of losing longs.
+
+`required_profit` will determine the profit (or loss) threshold below which a trade counts as a loss for the streak. This should normally not be set and defaults to 0.0 - meaning any trade closed with a negative profit counts towards the streak.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair for 12 candles after 3 consecutive losing trades on that pair, and stops trading altogether for 4 candles after 5 consecutive losing trades bot-wide.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxLosingStreak",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 5,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+        },
+        {
+            "method": "MaxLosingStreak",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": True,
+        },
+    ]
+```
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
